From 9f3b92d474982e9fefadabcdc53314dc3d75e2d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sento Daimon <sentodaimon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:52:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Coin Series: shorten genesis coinbase text to
 cs/<coin>/<env>/<H hash>

"coin-series/quarter/<env>/<hash>" made the genesis coinbase scriptSig 101 bytes
(limit 100), so the quarter chain rejected its own genesis (bad-cb-length) on
the first 7-day testnet. Test: every coin and network derives a valid genesis
from a real Bitcoin header.
---
 doc/coinseries/manual.md      |  2 +-
 doc/coinseries/spec.md        |  4 ++--
 src/kernel/chainparams.cpp    |  5 +++--
 src/test/coinseries_tests.cpp | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/coinseries/manual.md b/doc/coinseries/manual.md
index efea67b..f03c628 100644
--- a/doc/coinseries/manual.md
+++ b/doc/coinseries/manual.md
@@ -422,7 +422,7 @@ The genesis block is derived from the hash of a future Bitcoin block announced i
 1. Announce the launch reference Bitcoin block height H together with the software release. H is the Bitcoin height at release plus at least 432 blocks; about 72 hours on average, and the actual time may be shorter or longer
 2. H is recorded in the source as a consensus parameter. That block's hash cannot be known by anyone until the block is mined
 3. The genesis block is derived by a fixed formula from that hash
-    - Coinbase text = `"coin-series/<chain name>/" || reference block hash`
+    - Coinbase text = `"cs/<chain name>/<environment>/" || reference block hash (hex)` (short prefix keeps the coinbase script within 100 bytes)
     - Time = the reference block's timestamp
     - Difficulty bits = starting target, reward 0, exempt from proof-of-work check
 4. At startup a node takes the reference block hash as input and computes the genesis of all five chains itself. Participants verify the value on their own Bitcoin node or several block explorers
diff --git a/doc/coinseries/spec.md b/doc/coinseries/spec.md
index c70f2f4..8b3c68e 100644
--- a/doc/coinseries/spec.md
+++ b/doc/coinseries/spec.md
@@ -126,9 +126,9 @@ The txid covers version, all inputs, all outputs and lock time; input amounts an
 
 ## 10. Genesis (fair start)
 
-- With the release, the Bitcoin height H **(undecided)** is announced (release height + at least 432 blocks).
+- With the release, the Bitcoin height H is announced (release height + at least 432 blocks). The first 7-day testnet uses H = 973949 (already mined; the testnet carries no value).
 - Each node is started with `-beaconheader=<80-byte header of Bitcoin block H>`; on main and test the header must carry real Bitcoin proof of work (target ≤ 2^200).
-- Genesis per chain and environment: coinbase text `coin-series/<name>/<env>/<hash of block H>`, output `OP_RETURN` with value 0, time = time of block H, bits = start bits, nonce 0. Genesis hash uses the 180-byte header.
+- Genesis per chain and environment: coinbase text `cs/<name>/<env>/<hash of block H, hex>` (short prefix: the coinbase script must stay within 100 bytes), output `OP_RETURN` with value 0, time = time of block H, bits = start bits, nonce 0. Genesis hash uses the 180-byte header.
 - The genesis derived from the block H that remains in Bitcoin's final chain is canonical; blocks built on a replaced block H are invalid.
 - Releases after mining starts hardcode the hash of block H.
 
diff --git a/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp b/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp
index e6aed76..c8df302 100644
--- a/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp
+++ b/src/kernel/chainparams.cpp
@@ -836,8 +836,9 @@ public:
         const CScript genesis_script = CScript() << OP_RETURN;
         if (beacon) {
             // Genesis derived from Bitcoin block H (fixed formula, decided): coinbase text
-            // "coin-series/<coin>/<environment>/<block H hash>", time = block H time, bits = start target, reward 0.
-            const std::string genesis_msg = strprintf("coin-series/%s/%s/%s", std::string{info.name}, std::string{CoinEnvName(env)}, beacon->hash.GetHex());
+            // "cs/<coin>/<environment>/<block H hash>", time = block H time, bits = start target, reward 0.
+            // (Short prefix: the coinbase scriptSig must stay within 100 bytes; "coin-series/quarter/..." exceeded it.)
+            const std::string genesis_msg = strprintf("cs/%s/%s/%s", std::string{info.name}, std::string{CoinEnvName(env)}, beacon->hash.GetHex());
             const uint32_t genesis_bits = consensus.nASERTStartBits ? consensus.nASERTStartBits : UintToArith256(consensus.powLimit).GetCompact();
             genesis = CreateGenesisBlock(genesis_msg.c_str(), genesis_script, beacon->time, 0, genesis_bits, 1, /*genesisReward=*/0);
         } else {
diff --git a/src/test/coinseries_tests.cpp b/src/test/coinseries_tests.cpp
index b52c5dc..4784dcb 100644
--- a/src/test/coinseries_tests.cpp
+++ b/src/test/coinseries_tests.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,10 @@
 
 #include <test/util/setup_common.h>
 
+#include <consensus/tx_check.h>
